# Build context for the ROOT `Dockerfile` (the worker service).
#
# Docker reads the `.dockerignore` beside the context root, so `apps/api/.dockerignore`
# stops applying the moment the worker's context becomes the repo. Without this file
# the worker build uploads `apps/web/node_modules` and `.next` — hundreds of MB that
# the image never uses.
#
# `apps/api/.dockerignore` still governs the `api` service, whose context is still
# `apps/api`. Keep the two in step.

.git/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Never needed by the worker image.
apps/web/
PRD files/

# Python build noise (mirrors apps/api/.dockerignore).
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
apps/api/tests/

# Node build noise, in case anything else lands in the context later.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
